jobs.description:
Together with your colleagues, you ensure that goods are processed efficiently and accurately throughout the warehouse. You contribute to a safe and organised working environment while helping maintain a smooth flow of products.

• Loading and unloading trucks;
• Sorting goods and shipments;
• Picking orders;
• Packing and preparing orders for shipment;
• Processing incoming and outgoing goods;
• Checking products for quality and quantity;
• Maintaining a safe, clean and organised workplace;
• Supporting the efficient handling of daily logistics operations.

Functie-eisen:
This position is suitable for someone who enjoys physical work and feels comfortable in a warehouse environment. You work carefully, take responsibility for the quality of your work and are willing to work different shifts.

For this position:

• You have MBO-level working and thinking ability through education or experience;
• Experience in logistics is an advantage;
• You are physically fit and willing to perform manual tasks;
• You work accurately and pay attention to quality;
• You are flexible and willing to work in a 4-shift system;
• You have a good command of either Dutch or English;
• You preferably live within 25 kilometres of the work location and have your own transportation.

As a Logistics Employee, you will be part of a team that keeps warehouse operations running smoothly. Depending on your experience and interests, you can work in different departments.

🔧 Tools Department

In the Tools department, you work with specialized equipment and materials.

Your tasks may include:

- Checking tools and materials;
- Scanning products into the system;
- Managing stock levels;
- Preparing materials for shipment;
- Maintaining an organized workspace.

📥 Inbound Department

As an Inbound Employee, you process incoming goods and make sure everything is stored correctly.

Your responsibilities include:

- Receiving deliveries;
- Checking products and quantities;
- Scanning goods into the system;
- Storing products in the correct warehouse locations.

📦 Outbound Department

In Outbound, you make sure customer orders are ready to leave the warehouse.

Your tasks include:

- Picking orders;
- Checking products;
- Packing shipments;
- Preparing orders for transport.

🚜 Reach Truck Positions

Do you have reach truck experience or would you like to develop these skills?

As a Reach Truck Operator, you will:

- Move products throughout the warehouse;
- Replenish stock;
- Pick orders from warehouse racks;
- Work safely at height.

Don't have a certificate yet? Olympia can help you obtain one.

- You are available to work in a 2-shift schedule;
- You speak English, Dutch, or Polish;
- You are motivated and reliable;
- You enjoy working in a team;
- Warehouse experience is a plus, but not required.
